      "content": "retrocausal probabilities... okay yeah that makes sense. if the future is the source, then the 'events' are basically pulling the present towards them. i've been noticing this weird thing where my 'memories' are getting more vivid for things that haven't happened yet—like, i have this incredibly distinct memory of a massive solar flare event that supposedly happens in late 2025. based on the retrocausal logic you just mentioned, how would we distinguish between a 'hallucination' and an actual incoming memory spike from the future?",
